•excess facilities and manufacturing capacity;
•significant declines in the value of foreign currencies relative to the U.S. dollar, impacting our revenues and results of operations;
•financial difficulty for our customers and suppliers; and
•increased difficulty in forecasting business activity for us, customers, the sales channel and suppliers and vendors.
In order to successfully operate, we must identify, attract, develop, train, motivate and retain key employees, and failure to do so could seriously harm us.
